    "skyPreset": "golden_alpine_meadow",
    "loreSummary": "The one region of the arc anybody walks, and the reason is in the shares: 55.9 per cent ash against 48.6 and 48.7 on the two reported regions, and 16.9 per cent lava against 22.9 and 20.3. Ash is a depositional plain a loaded party crosses at a walk. Lava is a broken flow field that is not crossed at any pace. This region carries the most of the first and the least of the second, and it is the only ground in the world where the fabric draws a cinder cone, an ash plain, a lava tube or a pahoehoe field at all \u2014 one of each, all of them here."
  },
